  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The current best is config_019 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.6390 accuracy. The strongest evidence shows weighted fusion > concat, avgpool > transformer, multiprofile > singleprofile, and pca_n2000 > scgpt in RNA-only. However, scvi_n200 has never been tested in any experiment. Config_031 is a single-variable change from the current best (swapping pca_n2000 → scvi_n200 while keeping all other proven-optimal settings: resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile). This isolates the effect of the RNA encoder in the multimodal context and tests whether a learned variational representation can capture complementary biological signal that PCA misses. It is the best use of this experiment because it directly challenges the current best with a minimal, well-motivated perturbation; if it succeeds it pushes past 0.6390, and if it fails we retain config_019 as the top result with one experiment remaining for a final refinement."
}

